HandySend MTA integration
Upstream: https://gitcode.com/springtwr/HandySend
License: Apache License 2.0 (licenses/HandySend-Apache-2.0.txt)

The MTA protocol models, cryptography, GATT exchange, P2P orchestration,
WebSocket/HTTPS protocol, and streaming ZIP implementations retain their upstream
source. Host integration adapts preferences, directories, logging, history,
permission checks, native event registration and UI. MtaBleClient and
MtaBleReceiver adapt system scan and advertising resource ownership to coexist
with the existing protocols; their original packet builders/parsers are retained.

Brand and phone icons are from EasyShare (https://github.com/HotKids/EasyShare),
based on CatShare (https://github.com/kmod-midori/CatShare).
Copyright 2025 Midori Kochiya. MIT license: licenses/EasyShare-MIT.txt.

MTA TLS certificate support uses the unmodified LocalSend v1.18.2 cert.rs:
https://github.com/localsend/localsend/blob/v1.18.2/packages/core/src/crypto/cert.rs
LocalSend license: licenses/LocalSend-Apache-2.0.txt.
Only the certificate support module is linked; this does not replace the
application's existing LocalSend implementation.
